{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455957-aberrant-dependent-power-and-other-restricted-tag-uses","id":1455957,"title":"[Aberrant] Dependent Power and other Restricted Tag uses","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-01T14:49:21-07:00","id":1455957,"title":"[Aberrant] Dependent Power and other Restricted Tag uses","content":"I love the &quot;Restricted&quot; tag. Seriously, it enables us to do all sort of thematic things in the game.<br /> <br /> 1) So I was thinking about &quot;dependent&quot; powers, eg. Weathergirl has <i>Flight</i>, but can ONLY fly while her <i>Environmental Anima </i>power is active. So, she buys Flight as a <i>dependent power</i>. So, in your opinion, &quot;Dependent Power&quot; should be the same as &quot;Restricted -1&quot;, -2, or -3 Tag? Any particular reason?<br /> <br /> 2) I've stumbled in the concept of a nova that has Mega-Cunning, but does NOT have the Keen Senses Edges (and other similar ones, you got the Mega-Attb but not some/all the extra Edges or bonus(es) ). So, here we go again! To buy this Mega-Attribute without the Keen Senses, would that be &quot;Mega-Cunning&quot; with Restricted -1, -2, -3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T14:52:37-07:00","id":1455958,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure about question 2, but I think your example in question 1 would be easier if you bought flight as a technique for elemental anima. That said, if you wanted to stick with the restriction route I'd say -1 because it would only cost 1 technique to do something very similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T15:01:22-07:00","id":1455959,"title":"","content":"1) I think it should be -1. It\u2019s not expensive power and easy to keep active all time.<br /> <br /> 2) -1 and maybe not even that for the first dot in the mega attribute. An edge costs 1/4 of the dot cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T15:30:46-07:00","id":1455962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455957-aberrant-dependent-power-and-other-restricted-tag-uses?p=1455958#post1455958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure about question 2, but I think your example in question 1 would be easier if you bought flight as a technique for elemental anima. That said, if you wanted to stick with the restriction route I'd say -1 because it would only cost 1 technique to do something very similar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, I know about Techniques, but my question is about cases in which you really want a power to be un-useable in some circumstances (that's almost the opposite of Techniques, LoL, since I can use both at the same time). But thanks anyway! :-]<br /> <br /> 3) What about &quot;Dumbo Syndrome&quot;? e.g. My nova only can use his Environmental Anima if he has his &quot;magical&quot; amulet with him. No amulet, no Power. Actual examples: 3.1) can only Teleport if wearing a Magical Ring; 3.2) can only Quantum Attack using a Magical Wand; 3.3) can only use Environmental Anima while holding his Magical &quot;Wizards Staff&quot;. What would be each one of these? -1, -2, -3, why?<br /> <br /> Ps: I know there are Q-tech rules, but the point here is exactly not needing Q-Tech. It's just a psychological crutch for a nova that reaaaaly believes he can work magic, but will have to carve another wand if he loses or breaks his current one. He may need 1 hour tops to make &quot;the ritual&quot; to &quot;enchant a new wand&quot;, not even close to the work of making Q-Tech. Or even buy a wand from a &quot;witch&quot; he actually believes can do magic.<br /> <br /> 4) What about the reverse of 1), I mean, a &quot;Precluded Power&quot; (or even &quot;Precluding Power&quot;)? e.g.: JetHands can create jets of hot propulsion with his hands (Quantum Attack) aaaand... he can also use these as propulsion to fly (Flight). The problem is: <i>he can't do both at the same time</i>: every turn, he has to choose if he Flies or if he Attacks (he can never activate both powers at once). How would you model that? <b>4.1)</b> &quot;<b>Precluded </b>Power tag = this power that can never be used when <i>any other power of yours is</i> active&quot; (costs -1, -2, -3?); or <b>4.2) &quot;Precluding </b>Power = if this power is active, <i>you cannot use any other power of yours</i>&quot; (costs -1, -2, -3?); or even <b>4.3) </b>&quot;<b>Precluded Technique</b>&quot; (a tag to apply to the Technique Mega-Edge, or to Techniqued Powers, in which you <i>cannot </i>use <i>the </i>Techniqued(s) power(s) at the same time). What d'ya all think? What costs? \ud83e\udd14<br /> <br /> Dataweaver, maybe you'll like 4.3).<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","user":"Timecrafter","date":". 08-01-2021, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T16:01:49-07:00","id":1455966,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455957-aberrant-dependent-power-and-other-restricted-tag-uses#post1455957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the &quot;Restricted&quot; tag. Seriously, it enables us to do all sort of thematic things in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455957-aberrant-dependent-power-and-other-restricted-tag-uses#post1455957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">1) So I was thinking about &quot;dependent&quot; powers, eg. Weathergirl has <i>Flight</i>, but can ONLY fly while her <i>Environmental Anima </i>power is active. So, she buys Flight as a <i>dependent power</i>. So, in your opinion, &quot;Dependent Power&quot; should be the same as &quot;Restricted -1&quot;, -2, or -3 Tag? Any particular reason?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> This Tag basically already exists under Phasing. I see no reason applying it to other powers wouldn't work just fine, and it's listed as -1, which sounds right to me. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455957-aberrant-dependent-power-and-other-restricted-tag-uses#post1455957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">2) I've stumbled in the concept of a nova that has Mega-Cunning, but does NOT have the Keen Senses Edges (and other similar ones, you got the Mega-Attb but not some/all the extra Edges or bonus(es) ). So, here we go again! To buy this Mega-Attribute without the Keen Senses, would that be &quot;Mega-Cunning&quot; with Restricted -1, -2, -3?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Mechanically, you can't technically do this since you can't add Tags to Mega-Attributes, but if the SG allows it this seems reasonable enough. I'd peg it as a -1, since it effects less than half the power, IMO. If you think the Keen Senses are more like half the power it'd be -2.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455957-aberrant-dependent-power-and-other-restricted-tag-uses?p=1455962#post1455962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, I know about Techniques, but my question is about cases in which you really want a power to be un-useable in some circumstances (that's almost the opposite of Techniques, LoL, since I can use both at the same time). But thanks anyway! :-]<br /> <br /> 3) What about &quot;Dumbo Syndrome&quot;? e.g. My nova only can use his Environmental Anima if he has his &quot;magical&quot; amulet with him. No amulet, no Power. Actual examples: 3.1) can only Teleport if wearing a Magical Ring; 3.2) can only Quantum Attack using a Magical Wand; 3.3) can only use Environmental Anima while holding his Magical &quot;Wizards Staff&quot;. What would be each one of these? -1, -2, -3, why?<br /> <br /> Ps: I know there are Q-tech rules, but the point here is exactly not needing Q-Tech. It's just a psychological crutch for a nova that reaaaaly believes he can work magic, but will have to carve another wand if he loses or breaks his current one. He may need 1 hour tops to make &quot;the ritual&quot; to &quot;enchant a new wand&quot;, not even close to the work of making Q-Tech. Or even buy a wand from a &quot;witch&quot; he actually believes can do magic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Restriction is based on how much it, well, restricts you. If it restricts you meaningfully, but less than half the time, it's -1, if it's around half the time, it's -2, if it's more than half the time it's -3. Personally, I'd say that 'I need a wand' is probably -1, since it can be inconvenient in the moment but is easily solved by getting a new wand even if the wand is stolen or destroyed. 'I need THIS wand, specifically' is more like -2, because taking away the wand necessitates reclaiming it to regain the power and someone destroying the wand is even worse for you (maybe you need to find a nova with Transmutation to reconstruct it). A -3 'mystical' requirement is more like 'requires a full magic ritual' or 'requires diamond dust, which is consumed in using the power', or something similarly really restrictive, just needing to have an item would never cut it for -3 unless the item is, like, the size of a car or bigger (and maybe not even then).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455957-aberrant-dependent-power-and-other-restricted-tag-uses?p=1455962#post1455962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) What about the reverse of 1), I mean, a &quot;Precluded Power&quot; (or even &quot;Precluding Power&quot;)? e.g.: JetHands can create jets of hot propulsion with his hands (Quantum Attack) aaaand... he can also use these as propulsion to fly (Flight). The problem is: <i>he can't do both at the same time</i>: every turn, he has to choose if he Flies or if he Attacks (he can never activate both powers at once). How would you model that? <b>4.1)</b> &quot;<b>Precluded </b>Power tag = this power that can never be used when <i>any other power of yours is</i> active&quot; (costs -1, -2, -3?); or <b>4.2) &quot;Precluding </b>Power = if this power is active, <i>you cannot use any other power of yours</i>&quot; (costs -1, -2, -3?); or even <b>4.3) </b>&quot;<b>Precluded Technique</b>&quot; (a tag to apply to the Technique Mega-Edge, or to Techniqued Powers, in which you <i>cannot </i>use <i>the </i>Techniqued(s) power(s) at the same time). What d'ya all think? What costs? \ud83e\udd14<br /> <br /> Dataweaver, maybe you'll like 4.3).<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably also -1, just like #1, though it could be more if they're two powers that you would normally need at exactly the same time (a Quantum Attack and Quantum Field, for example). Definitely no double dipping on this one (you only get the Restriction on one of the two powers). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T16:16:40-07:00","id":1455968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deadmanwalking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455957-aberrant-dependent-power-and-other-restricted-tag-uses?p=1455966#post1455966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> This Tag basically already exists under Phasing. I see no reason applying it to other powers wouldn't work just fine, and it's listed as -1, which sounds right to me. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect!!! \\o/<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Mechanically, you can't technically do this since you can't add Tags to Mega-Attributes (...) </span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Yes you can, &quot;Power tags modify nova traits, particularly Quantum Powers but sometimes also Mega-Attributes and Mega-Edges&quot; (Aberrant p.199). In fact that's how you make a character that gives Super-Strenght to others, but doesn't have it himself: &quot;Mega-Might: Bestow Only&quot;.<br /> <br /> Thank you for the other answers, I agree with your take about Restrictions. :-]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T16:19:24-07:00","id":1455970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455957-aberrant-dependent-power-and-other-restricted-tag-uses?p=1455968#post1455968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes you can, &quot;Power tags modify nova traits, particularly Quantum Powers but sometimes also Mega-Attributes and Mega-Edges&quot; (Aberrant p.199). In fact that's how you make a character that gives Super-Strenght to others, but doesn't have it himself: &quot;Mega-Might: Bestow Only&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh wow, I totally missed that. Awesome.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T17:13:53-07:00","id":1455974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deadmanwalking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455957-aberrant-dependent-power-and-other-restricted-tag-uses?p=1455970#post1455970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh wow, I totally missed that. Awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it is! \\o/<br /> My eyes got shining when I noticed this and all the doors it opens.\ud83d\ude0d<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T12:04:35-07:00","id":1456084,"title":"","content":"I would use Boost (Might) Bestow Only for the Mega-Might for others, but tags can be added to mega attributes and mega edges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T13:27:06-07:00","id":1456088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>econclark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455957-aberrant-dependent-power-and-other-restricted-tag-uses?p=1456084#post1456084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would use Boost (Might) Bestow Only for the Mega-Might for others, but tags can be added to mega attributes and mega edges.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's another approach, with different results: using Boost you first give normal Might, then if the receiver gets to 5, it begins to become dots of Mega-Might. Using the other approach, the person simply gets Mega-Might immediately, but does not gain normal Attribute dots, ever.<br /> <br /> In fact, reading Boost made me think about using it in baselines: &quot; A nova cannot use Boost to increase a Mega-Attribute above her Quantum.&quot; So, does it mean I can't Boost a Baseline up to Mega-Might? not even Mega-Might 1?<br /> <br /> That's really odd for me, I liked to see drugs like Mite as Nova-Tech Compounds that emulate Might Boost... :/<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T15:18:15-07:00","id":1456090,"title":"","content":"My problem is I am not quite sure what the cost/duration of the Mega Might would be in your example....<br /> <br /> There are some other options (restricted Transformation) or perhaps the best for Mega Might would be Bestow only Mega Density Restricted (-2 no toughness)...pow. It also allows bypassing the normal Might requirements...so bonus <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T19:27:31-07:00","id":1456098,"title":"","content":"Bestow Mega-Might would also work, or should. By the rules it'd seem to last as long as the Bestow (which, by default starts as Maintained and is adjusted as normal with Tags...so it can't be forever, but could be up to several days).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T09:50:01-07:00","id":1456134,"title":"","content":"I totally agree it should work. I guess I would take the cost from the Q-tech section for Mega-Attributes (it does make it a bit expensive though). It is nice. I would still likely prefer to have boost as the vehicle for this as that is what it is designed for. A nova cannot use boost to gain mega attributes above HER quantum. I don't think this applies to others it is bestowed upon...it is limited by the Bestowing nova's quantum, not the receiving individual's quantum. Also, for boost, if you do Impose, you could also play with your psiad friends...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T07:20:42-07:00","id":1456236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455957-aberrant-dependent-power-and-other-restricted-tag-uses?p=1455968#post1455968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes you can, &quot;Power tags modify nova traits, particularly Quantum Powers but sometimes also Mega-Attributes and Mega-Edges&quot; (Aberrant p.199). In fact that's how you make a character that gives Super-Strenght to others, but doesn't have it himself: &quot;Mega-Might: Bestow Only&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting.<br /> There would be any cost?<br /> You can bestow your might to one person or more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25829-vjornin","name":"Vjornin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T13:32:42-07:00","id":1456261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vjornin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455957-aberrant-dependent-power-and-other-restricted-tag-uses?p=1456236#post1456236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting.<br /> There would be any cost?<br /> You can bestow your might to one person or more?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No inherent cost or limit to the number of targets if Bestowing a Mega-Attribute, but if you run completely out of Quantum they'd go away and the duration of the Bestow starts at Maintained as a default, so they go away if you are rendered unconscious in any way (including going to sleep). You also can't regain Quantum while maintaining a power and this would seem to count. <br /> <br /> So it's got a lot of other built in limitations but no direct cost or cap on number of people who can be effected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T16:41:37-07:00","id":1456270,"title":"","content":"I would say one, since Bestow says &quot;a target,&quot; and Mega-Attributes only enhance one person. As for cost, no there isn't a cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T20:01:49-07:00","id":1456273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455957-aberrant-dependent-power-and-other-restricted-tag-uses?p=1456270#post1456270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say one, since Bestow says &quot;a target,&quot; and Mega-Attributes only enhance one person. As for cost, no there isn't a cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bestow Only refers to it working 'on others', which IMO argues you can give it to multiple people, but it's definitely ambiguous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T06:16:42-07:00","id":1456302,"title":"","content":"If you want to prevent abuse, I think you should use some non-zero cost to bestow Mega-Attb. Probably 1q point, or if you want to maintain consistency across uses, use the same Q-Tech costs to activate Intrinsic Q-Tech Mega-Attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T15:13:49-07:00","id":1456316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1455957-aberrant-dependent-power-and-other-restricted-tag-uses?p=1456302#post1456302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to prevent abuse, I think you should use some non-zero cost to bestow Mega-Attb. Probably 1q point, or if you want to maintain consistency across uses, use the same Q-Tech costs to activate Intrinsic Q-Tech Mega-Attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>This winds up slightly odd since nothing else costs to Bestow, only to use, and Bestowing free powers already has explicit rules. I think the 'limiting it to one person at a time' option is probably better for limiting abuse than this.<br /> <br /> Though any way you look at it, not being able to regain Quantum normally while any of your Bestow effects are out there is a pretty big and meaningful limit, IMO","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T17:03:42-07:00","id":1456321,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of a cult leader that grants the followers Mega strength, dexterity or stamina for the rush of power. Or Mega compossure for the peace of mind.<br /> It's chosen ones would be addicted to it's pressence.<br /> Any day without it's touch would be like hell.<br /> <br /> So nice, so evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25829-vjornin","name":"Vjornin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T17:57:49-07:00","id":1456325,"title":"","content":"Looking at Bestow again, it explicitly says everything is based on the Nova's own stats rather than who it's bestowed on, so Boost would definitely also work if that's the desired effect, though Bestow on the Mega-Attributes themselves is probably easier if you already have the Mega-Attribute in question (a Cult Leader with Bestow on their Mega-Composure is a really great idea, thanks Vjornin).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26949-deadmanwalking","name":"Deadmanwalking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}